# Optional. Without it the app works normally, storing everything in this
# browser only — the sync panel simply reports that sync is not configured.
#
# To enable Google Drive sync:
#
#   1. console.cloud.google.com → create (or pick) a project
#   2. APIs & Services → Library → enable "Google Drive API"
#   3. APIs & Services → OAuth consent screen
#        - User type: External is fine for personal use
#        - Add yourself under "Test users"
#        - Scopes needed: .../auth/drive.file and .../auth/userinfo.email
#          (both non-sensitive, no review required)
#   4. Credentials → Create credentials → OAuth client ID
#        - Application type: Web application
#        - Authorised JavaScript origins: http://localhost:5173
#          (plus your real origin once deployed)
#   5. Copy the client ID below, into web/.env.local
#
# Heads-up: while the consent screen is in "Testing" status, Google expires the
# grant after about a week, so you will be asked to reconnect. Moving the app to
# "In production" is fine with only these two non-sensitive scopes and does not
# require a verification review.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
